    "result_text": "All 273 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners. When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, they're assigned a `membershipNumber` equal to one more than the current owner count, and that integer is returned in the owner response.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` (`integer`, `int32`) property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` at build time. MapStruct maps it automatically since the field names match.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 sets `owner.setMembershipNumber(findAllOwners().size() + 1)` before saving (after the conflict checks, before persistence).\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe new `Cp09Tests` (asserting two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) passes, along with the full suite (273 tests, 0 failures).",
